<title>BRAZIL: Brazil allows Korea Exchange Bank into country.</title>
<headline>Brazil allows Korea Exchange Bank into country.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's National Monetary Council has approved a proposal that allows the Korea Exchange Bank to set up operations in the country.</p>
<p>A statement issued after Wednesday's meeting of the council said the proposal had been passed. Officials did not comment on the decision after the meeting.</p>
<p>The Korea Exchange Bank stands to become the latest in a string of foreign banks given permission to operate in Brazil's booming banking sector.</p>
<p>The council decision must now be confirmed in a presidential decree.</p>
<p>(( -- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358))</p>
